content='```yaml\n---\n- name: Example Play\n  hosts: all\n\n  tasks:\n  - name: "Get efi path"\n    stat:\n      path: /sys/firmware/efi/efivars\n    register: efi_path\n\n  - name: "Remove unwanted grub.cfg on EFI systems"\n    file:\n      path: /boot/efi/EFI/{{ ansible_architecture }}/grub.cfg\n      state: absent\n\n  - name: "Install user template"\n    template:\n      src: templates/user.j2\n      dest: /etc/user.conf\n      mode: \'0644\'\n\n  - name: "EFI | add password"\n    lineinfile:\n      path: /sys/firmware/efi/efivars/SecureBoot-{{ ansible_architecture }}\n      line: "Password = password"\n      state: present\n\n  - name: "MBR | add password"\n    lineinfile:\n      path: /etc/mbr.conf\n      line: "Password = password"\n      state: present\n\n  - name: "Add --unrestricted"\n    replace:\n      path: /etc/user.conf\n      regexp: \'(^| )restricted( $| )\'\n      replace: \'\\1unrestricted\\2\'\n```\n\nThis Ansible Playbook will go through the tasks in the order specified. The `stat` module will get the EFI path and store it in a variable called `efi_path`. The `file` module will remove the `grub.cfg` file on EFI systems. The `template` module will install the `user` template. The `lineinfile` module will add the password to the EFI and MBR configurations. Finally, the `replace` module will add `--unrestricted` to the specified files.' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'llama3.1:8b', 'created_at': '2025-10-12T18:08:18.956766963Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 3198476763, 'load_duration': 106117640, 'prompt_eval_count': 425, 'prompt_eval_duration': 29130257, 'eval_count': 367, 'eval_duration': 3062571247, 'model_name': 'llama3.1:8b'} id='run--3194c0f2-b7bf-4137-9983-985aa0371bda-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 425, 'output_tokens': 367, 'total_tokens': 792}
