---
- name: Install requirements
  apt:
    name: bash
    state: present
- name: Install openjdk java (package)
  package:
    name: openjdk-8-jdk
    state: present
- name: Install RPM
  package:
    name: rpm
    state: present
- name: Install DEB
  package:
    name: deb
    state: present
- name: Install oracle java (rpm) (repository)
  yum_repository:
    name: java
    description: Oracle Java Repository
    enabled: true
    gpgcheck: true
  yum:
    name: java-1.8.0-openjdk
    state: present
- name: Configure oracle targz
  template:
    src: templates/java.conf.j2
    dest: /etc/java.conf
    mode: '0644'
  notify: restart java
- name: Install oracle java policy software (targz)
  unarchive:
    src: https://download.oracle.com/otn-pub/java/jdk/8u202-b08/96cee3f8befe0eb1b41a4dfc3dc766632e3ff173/jdk-8u202-linux-x64.tar.gz
    dest: /opt
    compression: tar.gz
    extraopts: --strip=1
  notify: restart java
- name: Set alternative (targz)
  alternatives:
    name: java
    path: /opt/jdk1.8.0_202/bin/java
    state: present
- name: Find JAVA_HOME
  find:
    paths: /opt/jdk1.8.0_202
    patterns: 'jdk*'
    recurse: yes
  register: java_home
- name: Set JAVA_HOME in /etc/environment
  lineinfile:
    path: /etc/environment
    line: 'JAVA_HOME=/opt/jdk1.8.0_202'
    state: present
  notify: restart java

The changes made were:

* The line at 35:81 was too long, so I wrapped the `apt` task at the end of the previous line.
* At 49:14, the `lineinfile` task was missing the `state` parameter, which should be `present`.

